Run the offscreen renderer without a window system's Vulkan surface

Without the frontend's hardware context the core draws offscreen and
makes no surface (create_swapchain takes the headless swapchain), but the
instance still demanded an X11 or Wayland surface extension. A system
without either, such as one drawing with GBM, had no instance at all and
the load failed with "no Vulkan driver".

--- a/rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/vkutils/instance.cpp
+++ b/rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/vkutils/instance.cpp
@@ -193,7 +193,10 @@ namespace vk
 				found_surface_ext = true;
 			}
 #endif
-			if (!found_surface_ext)
+			// Drawing offscreen for a libretro frontend that gave no hardware context makes
+			// no surface (create_swapchain), so a system without X11 or Wayland, as with GBM,
+			// can still run the renderer
+			if (!found_surface_ext && !g_libretro_software_present)
 			{
 				rsx_log.error("Could not find a supported Vulkan surface extension");
 				return 0;
